 "derivations": {
  "verticalLayout": "Head: chin 1.464 to crown 1.700 = 0.236 m, i.e. 7.2 head-heights in a 1.700 m figure. The skin skull is 0.206 m (half-height 0.103) with the 30 mm hair cap above it, so the top of the modelled hair lands exactly on crownHeight. Eyes at 1.580, shoulder line 1.400, hips 0.856. Both character builders place the collar, tie, arms, glasses, moustache and hair from these values, and Tools/audit_character_spec.py checks the sums.",
  "headVolume": "Head height 0.236 m = skull 0.206 m + hair cap 0.030 m. Skull half-height 0.103 m, so the skull centre sits at crownHeight - hairCapThickness - skullHalfHeight = 1.567 m and the top of the hair lands exactly on crownHeight (1.700 m). The face is clean-shaven but for the moustache."
 }
